<div class="posts">
<article class="post" data-cat="path"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Second jobs</span><span>7 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-second-path/">Why people take a second job</a></h3><p>Additional work may support household costs, build experience in a preferred field or fit around study, caregiving and other commitments, depending on hours and pay… <a class="read-more" href="/article-second-path/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="path"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Where to look</span><span>6 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-where-to-look/">How to search for remote work</a></h3><p>Remote searches work best when a job title, location, work arrangement and available hours are used together instead of relying on broad work-from-home keywords alone… <a class="read-more" href="/article-where-to-look/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="hiring"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Work types</span><span>6 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-three-arrangements/">How remote, online and flexible work differ</a></h3><p>Remote describes location, online describes how work is delivered, and flexible describes hours or workload. These distinctions help narrow suitable postings before applying for work… <a class="read-more" href="/article-three-arrangements/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="market"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">The market</span><span>6 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-what-vacancies-mean/">What the remote job market looks like in Canada</a></h3><p>Remote work is established in Canada, but remote openings remain a small share of all postings. Occupation, province and experience influence each search and outcome… <a class="read-more" href="/article-what-vacancies-mean/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="hiring"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Before you apply</span><span>7 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-read-a-remote-ad/">How to read a remote job posting</a></h3><p>A clear remote posting identifies the employer, permitted work location, hours, pay and employment status, helping applicants assess the position before applying or sharing information… <a class="read-more" href="/article-read-a-remote-ad/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="hiring"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Application</span><span>5 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-remote-cv/">Résumés for online and remote work</a></h3><p>Remote employers often assess relevant results, written communication, digital tools and the ability to work with limited on-site supervision. A focused résumé surfaces these details… <a class="read-more" href="/article-remote-cv/">Read more</a></p></article>
<article class="post" data-cat="pay"><div class="meta"><span class="cat">Pay</span><span>7 min</span></div><h3><a href="/article-pay-and-province/">What a second paycheque changes</a></h3><p>A second paycheque can change payroll deductions and tax withholding. Minimum wage, employment status and the employer’s province also affect how pay is handled overall… <a class="read-more" href="/article-pay-and-province/">Read more</a></p></article>
